# XSH pthread_join()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every target is a joinable thread other than the caller, joined once
# (the other cases are undefined behaviour). Waits that the text leaves
# unbounded are left to the driver's timeout.

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.001
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       pthread_join() on a thread that is still running waits for it:
           it returns 0 only after the target (sleeping 300 ms first) has
           set a flag and ended, and gives the target's value.
test       t/001-waits.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.002
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       pthread_join() on a thread that has (in all likelihood) already
           terminated returns 0 and the thread's value.
note       The target signals just before returning and the caller waits
           200 ms more; if it has not quite ended, the call simply waits,
           which the assertion also allows.
test       t/002-already-terminated.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.003
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A non-null value_ptr receives the value the target passed to
           pthread_exit() (a pointer to an object, or a null pointer) or
           returned from its start routine; with a null value_ptr the join
           succeeds as well.
test       t/003-value.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.004
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.3
class      required
since      2001
says       When pthread_join() returns 0 the target has terminated: the
           cleanup handler (200 ms long) and the thread-specific data
           destructor (100 ms long) it ran on pthread_exit() have both
           finished.
test       t/004-terminated-on-return.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.005
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      2001
says       A signal caught by the joining thread (SIGUSR1, handler installed
           without SA_RESTART) while it waits does not make pthread_join()
           return EINTR: it returns 0 with the value once the target ends.
test       t/005-no-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_join.006
anchor     functions/pthread_join.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When a thread blocked in pthread_join() is canceled, the target
           stays joinable: the canceled thread ends with PTHREAD_CANCELED,
           and a later pthread_join() of the target returns 0 and its
           value.
note       Cancellation is acted on in pthread_join(), a cancellation point
           (XSH 2.9.5.2); the target is kept blocked until then, so the
           join cannot succeed first.
test       t/006-cancel-not-detach.c
